From cff02d5abecd0e454b8685aef1b9b14b24ee91ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:48:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] pinctrl: meson: add Amlogic A4 style pin controller
 driver

The Amlogic A4, A9, S6 and S7 SoCs use a new pin controller binding
("amlogic,pinctrl-a4" and friends): the pin groups are not described by
the driver anymore but by "pinmux" properties in the device tree, each
entry holding the pin number (bank << 8 | offset) and its mux value, and
every GPIO bank is a sub-node with its own "gpio", "mux" and optional
"ds" register regions.

Add a pin controller and GPIO driver for this binding, following the
Linux pinctrl-amlogic-a4 driver, including the tables of the pins whose
mux lives in the registers of another bank (A9, S6, S7).

The pin controller handles the pin group nodes referenced by pinctrl-N
properties: mux, bias, drive strength and the input/output properties.
Each GPIO bank sub-node is bound as a GPIO controller, named after the
bank (GPIOX_, GPIOH_, ...), requesting a GPIO switches the pin back to
its GPIO function.

The pinctrl-meson core is now only built for the drivers selecting
PINCTRL_MESON, it is not needed by this driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
